{
  "dom_id": "step-q92197",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/0f2da39fd7b29aeae45dc320fd581a7609c294b2c7680f72f6da37e9a2cba023.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?",
  "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{2}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $2$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/5b0cc16df0963c00eb9408d8c9d302144310b84070a2419d74ad15973b54cbb3.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{4}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/947ff1d81f16e2b2e0ce65c7b4b3b0475ebc9c80554d3b530d553c1bf2a674ba.png)",
